From 225aec89be4a199650ff162b327a41052d95c69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 2026 07:38:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] LocalDisplayAdapter: pre-set committedState to ON for first
 internal display

On devices where the vendor HWC does not implement getDisplayConnectionType
(e.g. HIDL HWC 2.1 as shipped on many MediaTek devices), SurfaceFlinger
powers on the built-in display during its own initialisation, before
LocalDisplayAdapter exists.  mCommittedState is initialised to STATE_UNKNOWN
and stays there until the first requestDisplayStateLocked call from
DisplayPowerController, which only arrives after system_server has fully
booted -- potentially 10-20 minutes into first boot.

During this window:
- PowerManagerService: 'Tried to acquire wake lock for invalid display: 0'
  -- cannot hold the screen on after boot animation exits
- DeviceStateManagerService: 'Cannot notify device state info change before
  the initial state has been committed'
- Touch ICs that gate on DRM notifier callbacks (e.g. chipone_tddi via
  tct_display_touch_interface) interpret STATE_UNKNOWN as display-off and
  keep themselves suspended -- touch is dead until committedState commits

The fix: for the first internal display, initialise mCommittedState to
STATE_ON at construction time.  SurfaceFlinger always powers on the
primary display before LocalDisplayAdapter is created, so this matches
physical reality.  The subsequent requestDisplayStateLocked call will
update the state normally from that point.
---
 .../android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
index 6865a23a7..0b238d011 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
@@ -276,6 +276,19 @@ final class LocalDisplayAdapter extends DisplayAdapter {
             mBacklightAdapter = mInjector.getBacklightAdapter(displayToken, isFirstDisplay,
                     mSurfaceControlProxy);
             mActiveSfDisplayModeAtStartId = dynamicInfo.activeDisplayModeId;
+
+            // On devices where the vendor HWC does not implement getDisplayConnectionType
+            // (e.g. HIDL HWC 2.1), SurfaceFlinger powers on the built-in display during
+            // its own init before LocalDisplayAdapter exists.  mCommittedState stays at
+            // STATE_UNKNOWN until the first requestDisplayStateLocked call, which only
+            // arrives after system_server has fully booted.  During that window
+            // PowerManagerService cannot acquire a wake lock for display 0 (invalid display
+            // state), so the screen goes dark immediately after the boot animation ends.
+            // Pre-set mCommittedState to STATE_ON for the first internal display to reflect
+            // the physical reality: SurfaceFlinger already powered it on.
+            if (isFirstDisplay && staticDisplayInfo.isInternal) {
+                mCommittedState = Display.STATE_ON;
+            }
         }
 
         @Override
